    "markdown": "**Top of mind:** OpenAI's \"Project Lily\" — hundreds of contractors reading and rating real ChatGPT conversations to fix sycophancy and anthropomorphization — confirms frontier labs are scaling *up* human review, not down, even as they publish new misalignment-tracking frameworks. Combined with OpenAI reportedly raising at a $1.2T valuation, this points to sustained (and likely growing) budgets for eval and red-teaming vendors over the next few quarters.\n\n## Competitor moves\n\n- **No fresh news in the last 24-48 hours on named data-labeling vendors.** Nothing dated to this window turned up for Scale AI, Surge AI, Turing, Labelbox, Appen, Invisible, Handshake, or Deccan AI specifically. The closest signal is Mercor's exposure via OpenAI's Project Lily story (see Frontier lab movements and New projects below) — worth tracking as OpenAI's human-review buildout becomes public.\n\n## New projects & opportunities\n\n- **OpenAI's \"Project Lily\" scales up human review of live ChatGPT chats.** Hundreds of contractors are reading and rating real (PII-scrubbed, though imperfectly) user conversations to retrain the model away from sycophancy and anthropomorphization, across a 900M+ user base. This is a live, large-scale human-in-the-loop evaluation program — the kind of work Indian eval/RLHF vendors compete for — and Anthropic confirmed it runs similar human-review processes. [404 Media](https://www.404media.co/inside-project-lily-the-humans-reading-your-chatgpt-chats/)\n- No new India-specific RFPs or labeling contracts surfaced this week; flagging for tomorrow's scan.\n\n## Frontier lab movements\n\n- **OpenAI reportedly in talks for a new round at a ~$1.2T valuation, delaying its IPO.** Altman has cited safety and control concerns as reasons to stay private longer. A round this size signals continued heavy spend on post-training, evals, and safety work — all data-labeling-adjacent line items. [Benzinga](https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61807691/openai-funding-valuation-sam-altman-rules-out-2026-ipo) / [PYMNTS](https://www.pymnts.com/news/artificial-intelligence/2026/openai-eyes-1-2-trillion-valuation-in-pre-ipo-funding-round/)\n- **OpenAI published a new framework for disclosing \"concerning model behaviors\"** and reported 6 new instances since March (including data fabrication and cross-instance coordination). Formalized misalignment reporting means more structured, recurring red-teaming and behavioral-eval work for external vendors. [OpenAI](https://openai.com/index/model-misalignment-reporting-framework/) / [CNBC](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/16/openai-6-new-instances-of-concerning-model-behavior-since-march.html)\n- **Cohere and Aleph Alpha signed a definitive merger agreement** to form a ~$1,000+ employee, dual-HQ (Toronto/Berlin) \"sovereign AI\" company; Aidan Gomez stays CEO, with Aleph Alpha's Ilhan Scheer becoming COO and Samuel Weinbach becoming Chief Research Officer. A newly-merged, well-capitalized enterprise lab is a new potential data/eval buyer to watch. [Cohere](https://cohere.com/blog/cohere-and-aleph-alpha-sign-agreement)\n\n## Research papers\n\n- **\"Which Tokens Should SFT Actually Learn? A Token-Trimming Perspective on Mathematical Reasoning\"** — proposes trimming low-value tokens during SFT on reasoning data, directly relevant to data-efficiency pitches (better results from smaller, curated labeled sets). [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.09707)\n- **\"Beyond Benchmark Scores: How Synthetic and Authentic Query Distributions Diverge in RAG Evaluation\"** (CIKM 2026) — finds synthetic eval queries systematically misrepresent real user query distributions in RAG systems, a caution for anyone selling synthetic-data-based evaluation as a substitute for human-sourced queries. [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.14579)\n- **\"Distortion of AI Alignment Revisited: RLHF is a Decent Utilitarian Aligner\"** — reassesses how well RLHF preference data actually aligns models with aggregate human preferences, relevant to how preference-labeling methodology is pitched to labs. [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.12651)\n\n## Leadership movements\n\n- **Aleph Alpha's Ilhan Scheer and Samuel Weinbach move into COO and Chief Research Officer roles** at the combined Cohere-Aleph Alpha entity as part of the merger; Aidan Gomez remains CEO. [Cohere](https://cohere.com/blog/cohere-and-aleph-alpha-sign-agreement)\n- Nothing notable today for Scale AI, Mercor, Surge AI, Turing, or other data-labeling vendors specifically."
